### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `div` with some content) that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or rotation axis to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;          /* width of the card */
    height:360px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hand icon on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Inner wrapper that will rotate ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* place it behind the front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* flip the inner wrapper */
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Optional styling for content ---------- */
.card h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:#333;
}
.card p {
    margin:0;
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#666;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Here is the other side.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | The page is centered using Flexbox. |
| **2** | `.card` sets the perspective so that 3D transforms look realistic. |
| **3** | `.card-inner` is the element that actually rotates. |
| **4** | `.card-front` and `.card-back` are positioned absolutely on top of each other. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away. |
| **5** | On hover, the inner wrapper rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, flipping the card. |
| **6** | Simple typography styling for demo purposes. |

You can change:

- `perspective` value for more or less depth.
- `transform:rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` if you want a vertical flip.
- Add more content or images inside the faces.

Enjoy experimenting!
